{"id": "197489", "revid": "107092", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=197489", "title": "Kashimbila Game Reserve", "text": "Kashimbila Game Reserve is in Taraba State of Nigeria.\nUnderstand.\nThe Kashimbila Game Reserve is located in Takum local government area, southwestern flank of Taraba State, Nigeria, just close to the Cameroon border. It is a tourist attraction sight with trees and animals.\nHistory.\nThe game reserve was established in 1977.\nLandscape.\nThe game reserve is generally greeny in most parts of the year. It covers an area of 1,072.26 km\u00b2.\nClimate.\nThe climate is tropical.\nGet around.\nThe most reserve is navigable by foot and by means of a jeep.\nStay safe.\nBeing that the reserve is not properly managed, safety is not guaranteed to any tourist, so one should go prepared for the expected. It is advisable that one goes with at least two hunter tour guides."}
